  "scenario": "**Patient:** Eli Johnson, nine-year-old boy with severe hypoxic-ischemic encephalopathy, epilepsy, tracheostomy, and lifelong ventilator dependence.\n\n**Admission:** PICU day six, admitted with severe pneumonia and acute-on-chronic respiratory failure. He initially stabilized but has not returned to his home baseline ventilator settings. The team is worried he may not survive this admission or recover to his prior functional baseline.\n\n**Family context:** Marissa Johnson (thirty-six) is Eli's mother and primary caregiver. She has managed Eli's ventilator, G-tube feeds, seizure medications, and home nursing schedule since infancy. Eli lives with Marissa and his twelve-year-old sister Nia. Eli's grandmother Denise is a close presence who believes any limitation of interventions would be \"giving up.\"\n\n**Why this conversation now:** Marissa asked to speak with the PICU fellow after hearing the attending say \"We need to talk about the bigger picture.\" She is worried the team is giving up on Eli. She has never had a formal goals-of-care conversation.",
